      "body": "## Purpose\n\nOn RDNA (gfx12), `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1` always puts `ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN` first, and\n`VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION=0` has no effect there. That leaves no way to avoid\nthis one kernel without turning off aiter entirely (and losing its other Triton paths such as\nlinear GEMM).\n\nThe original LDS-overflow crash from #56021 is fixed on the kernel side by ROCm/aiter#4868\n(shipped in aiter v0.1.23), and AMD selects this backend on gfx12 by default on purpose. So\nthis PR is now deliberately narrow:\n\n- **Default unchanged**: with the variable unset, RDNA still prefers `ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN`.\n- **Explicit opt-out honored**: `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION=0` drops only this\n  backend on RDNA. This matters while the kernel does not support multimodal inputs and\n  silently produces wrong attention output for them (per AMD in #56021).\n\n`is_rdna_unified_attn_enabled()` uses `envs.is_set()` to tell \"unset\" from \"explicitly 0\".\n\nRelated: #56021\n\n## Not a duplicate\n\nSearched open PRs for `56021 in:body`, `ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN RDNA`,\n`VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION`, `gfx12 unified attention` and `rdna4 aiter attention`.\nNone changes how this variable is read on RDNA. #61332 and #42798 also edit\n`_get_backend_priorities()`, but for the CDNA ordering of `ROCM_AITER_FA` / `ROCM_ATTN`, and keep\nthe RDNA branch as is; whichever lands second needs a trivial rebase. ROCm/aiter#4868 fixes the\nkernel's LDS budget and does not touch vLLM's backend selection.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` (ruff 0.14.0, as pinned in pre-commit): pass.\n- `tests/v1/attention/test_rocm_attention_backends_selection.py::test_rdna_unified_attn_backend_opt_out`\n  covers unset / `0` / `1` through the real env handling (`refresh_env_variables()` +\n  `_get_backend_priorities()`), mocking only the RDNA/aiter detection.\n- **Not run locally**: this file is ROCm-only (module-level skip), and I do not have a ROCm\n  device. I'd appreciate an `/amd-ci run`.\n\nNo model output changes when the variable is unset (default path unchanged), so no eval was run.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nThis change was written with AI assistance (Claude Code). I reviewed every changed line and\ncan explain and defend the change.\n",
