      "body": "@amd-xavierwang thanks for ROCm/aiter#4868, that fixes the crash from #56021 at the source.\n\nI've narrowed this PR accordingly: the RDNA default (prefer `ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN` when aiter\nis on) is left as is, and the only change is that an explicit\n`VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION=0` now opts out of this one backend. Given your note that\nthe kernel doesn't support multimodal inputs yet and returns wrong output for them, that seems\nlike a useful escape hatch that keeps aiter's other Triton paths on.\n\nThe test is ROCm-only so I couldn't run it locally. Could someone with access trigger\n`/amd-ci run`?\n",
